  "description": "*****UNDER OFFER SIMILAR PROPERTIES REQUIRED******\n\n\nO'Connor Murphy Auctioneers are delighted to bring to the market 68 Oakleigh Wood, Dooradoyle. This spacious three-bedroom ground floor apartment with its own-door entrance offers bright, beautifully presented accommodation together with the rare benefit of a private, fully enclosed rear garden. Located in one of Limerick's most sought-after residential areas, this property is ideal for first-time buyers, those trading down, or anyone wishing to settle in a mature, convenient setting within walking distance of a host of amenities including the Crescent Shopping Centre, excellent schools and University Hospital Limerick.\n\nACCOMMODATION:\n\nThe property comprises of an entrance hallway, a bright open-plan living/dining room and kitchen, three bedrooms (main bedroom with ensuite and direct access to the rear garden) and a main bathroom.\n\n\nGROUND FLOOR:\n\nEntrance Hallway - Feature black and white patterned tiled flooring with access to all principal rooms\nOpen Plan Kitchen/Living/Dining Room - Bright and spacious open-plan living and dining space with wooden flooring, feature fireplace and recess lighting. \nKitchen - Fitted wall and floor units in a striking teal finish with marble-effect worktops and herringbone tiled splashback. \nBedroom 1 - Rear facing double room with wooden flooring, built-in wardrobes and ensuite. Sliding patio door opening directly onto the private rear garden\nEnsuite - Shower room with corner shower enclosure, electric shower, WC and vanity WHB. Grey and teal tiling with tiled flooring\nBedroom 2 - Rear facing double room with wooden flooring\nBedroom 3 - Front facing room with laminate flooring, currently in use as a home office. Ideal for those working from home\nMain Bathroom - Spacious main bathroom comprising bath with shower over and glass screen, WC and vanity WHB with storage. Grey metro tiled walls and mosaic tiled flooring\n\n\nEXTERIOR:\n\nFront - Own-door entrance with attractive brick and cut-stone facade, outdoor lighting and designated parking\nRear garden - Fully enclosed, private and beautifully maintained rear garden with low-maintenance artificial lawn bordered by railway sleepers, generous stone patio area, mature tree and established planting. Garden shed and outdoor lighting. Accessed via sliding door from the main bedroom\n\n\nLOCATION:\n\n68 Oakleigh Wood is located in a mature, highly sought-after development just off the main Dooradoyle Road. The property is ideally positioned within walking distance of the Crescent Shopping Centre and a number of well-regarded primary and secondary schools, including Crescent College Comprehensive. The Rosedale Centre, with its convenience store, pharmacy and medical centre, is also within a short stroll. University Hospital Limerick and Raheen Business Park are both close by, making this an excellent base for those working in the area, while sports enthusiasts are well served by nearby clubs and leisure facilities. The location also offers easy access to the M20 Cork motorway, the M7 Dublin motorway and the N18 Shannon/Galway road.\n\n\n\n\nServices:\n\nGas Heating \nDouble Glazed Windows\nDesignated Parking Space\nManagement Fees Incurred\nAccommodation\n\n Note: \nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only. Property Reference :OMUR6759\nDIRECTIONS:\nV94 E138",
